{"book":19,"chapter":89,"context":{"chapter":89,"title":"Where Are Your Promises to David?","summary":"Ethan celebrates God's faithfulness and his covenant promising David an everlasting throne, then laments that the crown lies in the dust, and asks where God's former love has gone. Book III closes.","background":"Title: 'Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite.' Ethan, like Heman, was known for wisdom (1 Kings 4:31). The psalm restates God's oath in 2 Samuel 7 (vv. 19–37), then mourns the king's defeat (vv. 38–45), likely the fall of the Davidic monarchy. Verse 52 is the doxology ending Book III.","customs":[],"watchFor":["'Faithfulness' and 'mercy' recur throughout.","'He shall cry unto me, Thou art my father' (v. 26); 'my firstborn' (v. 27)."],"connections":["2 Samuel 7:12-16","1 Kings 4:31","Acts 13:22","Revelation 1:5"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["מַשְׂכִּיל","maskil","H4905","HNtmsa","a poem"],["לְאֵיתָן","le'eitan","H387","HR/Npm","of Ethan"],["הָאֶזְרָחִי","ha'ezrachi","H250","HTd/Ngmsa","the Ezrachite"]]},"1":{"w":[["חַסְדֵי","chasdei","H2617","HNcmpc","[the] covenant loyalti<es> of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["עוֹלָם","olam","H5769","HNcmsa","forever"],["אָשִׁירָה","'ashirah","H7891","HVqc1cs","I will sing"],["לְדֹר","ledor","H1755","HR/Ncmsa","to a generation"],["וָדֹר","vador","H1755","HC/Ncmsa","and a generation"],["אוֹדִיעַ","'odia'","H3045","HVhi1cs","I will make known"],["אֱמוּנָתְךָ","'emunatekha","H530","HNcfsc/Sp2ms","faithfulness your"],["בְּפִי","befi","H6310","HR/Ncmsc/Sp1bs","with mouth my"]],"x":[[19101001,19101001,12],[19089008,19089008,9],[19119090,19119090,7],[25003023,25003023,7],[19089033,19089033,6],[19036005,19036005,5],[19089004,19089005,5],[19059016,19059016,4],[19086012,19086013,4],[19088011,19088011,4]],"xn":16},"2":{"w":[["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","for"],["אָמַרְתִּי","'amarti","H559","HVqp1cs","I have said"],["עוֹלָם","olom","H5769","HNcmsa","forever"],["חֶסֶד","chesed","H2617","HNcmsa","covenant loyalty"],["יִבָּנֶה","yiban